  "body": "## What\n\nA reviewable pilot for #853: a **data-driven language registry**, a Simplified\nChinese catalogue (English as source and fallback), a bundled CJK font, and a\nlive language picker. Doubles as an architecture proposal for the issue's open\nquestions. Opened as a **draft** because #853 is currently `P?` (paused) —\nplease set a priority / pick a mechanism before treating this as ready.\n\n## Scope\n\n### One registry, not a hardcoded pair\n\n`Lang` is a descriptor; every shipped language is one row of `REGISTRY` in\n`crates/i18n`. `Lang::ALL`, locale parsing, the parse-once catalogue cache and\nthe View door's picker all derive from that row — adding a language is a\ncatalogue file plus a row, with no change to lookup logic or any call site. A\ntest names any inconsistent row (duplicate tag, missing native name, tag that\ndoes not round-trip, unreadable catalogue).\n\n### Coverage\n\n`assets/i18n/zh-CN.toml` now ships **3,638 strings**. The surface covered by\nthis branch includes:\n\n- ribbon commands, groups and section captions; tree section headers and\n  literal rows (user names are never translated); machine and operation tabs\n- shared property vocabulary, operation headers, help/hover text, consequence\n  lines, action-bar hover/disabled reasons, status banner lines\n- static literals at direct egui call sites (`on_hover_text`, `label`, `button`,\n  `checkbox`, `menu_item`, `Label/RichText/Button::new`) — 653+ call sites\n- 106 frequently used UI string constants\n- **dynamic `format!` templates** through `tf()`: the template is the catalogue\n  key, so Chinese can reorder words; arguments are pre-rendered and substituted\n  in the translated template's placeholder order. 1,553 unique templates in\n  `crates/app` and 766 in `crates/ui` are routed, with **0 missing keys**\n- **status line, refusal and page-label templates** in `crates/ui` (72 call\n  sites across 32 files), including the timed import/refresh line where the\n  verb is translated at its own seam\n\nCoverage is enforced structurally: scripts extract static strings reaching\n`tr()` and dynamic templates reaching `tf()`, and confirm 0 missing keys.\n\n### Font\n\n`assets/ui/fonts/NotoSansSC-Regular-Subset.ttf` is Noto Sans SC 400 subset to\nGB2312 + punctuation (8,090 code points, 2.3 MB, OFL 1.1), embedded with\n`include_bytes!`. A test reads the TTF's `cmap` directly to prove every shipped\nstring is covered.\n\n### Language choice\n\nFollows the system locale (`LC_ALL`, `LC_MESSAGES`, `LANG`); `CAMCRAFT_LANG`\noverrides for one run; the View door's **Language** list switches live and\npersists to `prefs.json`. The list is generated from `Lang::ALL`, so a new\nregistry row appears there without a UI change.\n\n## Deliberately not translated\n\nNothing that must never be localised is routed through the catalogue:\nG-code, CL, project files, `.mch`/`.cps`, MCP tool names and JSON, parsed log\nlines and test goldens. English is the key, so a miss shows English — never a\nkey or a blank. Also left alone: wordless concatenation templates (`{n}`,\ndimension-only rows) and format names/paths. Refusal **codes** matched by\n`starts_with()` stay in English as stable identity, while their displayed\nsentences are translated and the match accepts either form — a regression\ntest proves a translated refusal still retires in every language.\n\n## Integration note\n\nRebased onto current `main`. The upstream refactor moved the operation header\ninto `egui_app/op_page/header.rs`; commit `57468bfa` re-applies the translations\nthere. `08c8c91f` adds `Undercut` / `V-Carve`. `e2ab79fe` expands static\ncoverage; `19eed997` adds `tf()` and translates the dynamic UI layer;\n`89172375` / `b818cf79` translate app-layer messages and labels drawn outside\n`tr()` helpers. One head adds the data-driven registry and the status/label seam; the\nlatest adds translated refusal heads (commit `0093244c`) with a stable-code\nmatch that survives a language switch.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-i18n -p camcraft-app --all-targets` — passes, no warnings\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-i18n` — 12 passed + 1 doctest (incl. the new registry-law test)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib i18n_tests` — 4 passed\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib fonts::tests` — 4 passed (glyph coverage of every shipped string)\n- `python3 scripts/i18n/check.py assets/i18n/zh-CN.toml` — 3,638 strings, 0 errors\n- static + dynamic coverage scans: 0 strings reaching `tr()`/`tf()` without a Chinese entry in `crates/ui` and `crates/app`\n\n## Design docs\n\n`docs/I18N.md` and `docs/decisions/853-ui-translations.md` record the\narchitecture, the registry law, the measurements and the deliberate scope\nboundary.\n",
